msgid "The database to search, by the order this module's docstring describes."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.input_db.copy_default_input_db_into:3 of
msgid ""
"`copy_default_input_db` puts the example one level down, as `input_db/`, "
"because its caller owns a formats repository and wants a database inside "
"it. `init-input-db` builds the database directory itself, so the example "
"has to land in that directory rather than beside it — and it lands on top"
" of the header-only files already written there, which is what makes the "
"seeded and the empty database the same shape."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.input_db.resolve_input_db:3 of
msgid ""
"``config`` is an already-built :class:`~freeports_dev.config.DevConfig` "
"when the caller has one; the pytest plugin has none to build it from, so "
"it falls back to whatever the process resolved."
msgstr ""

